/-
# `SL₃(ℤ)` as a quotient of the modular group (Kourovka Notebook Problem 14.49)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.49 (M. Conder): is `SL₃(ℤ)` a quotient of
the modular group `PSL₂(ℤ) ≅ C₂ ∗ C₃`, that is, can `SL₃(ℤ)` be generated by two elements of orders
`2` and `3`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SL3IntTwoThreeGenerationKourovka14Problem49Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.49 (M.
Conder). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701034 (`KOU-14.49`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Stated in the problem's own reformulation: generation by an element of order `2` and an element of
order `3` (a quotient of `C₂ ∗ C₃` is generated by elements of orders dividing `2` and `3`, and
`SL₃(ℤ)` is not cyclic).
-/

/-- **$(2,3)$-generation of $\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ (Kourovka 14.49).** The statement that
there are $a, b \in \mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ such that $a$ has order $2$, $b$ has order $3$, and
$a$ and $b$ generate $\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$.

Kourovka Notebook Problem 14.49 (M. Conder) asks whether $\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ is a quotient
of the modular group $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \cong C_2 \ast C_3$; since
$\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ is not cyclic, this is equivalent to the statement above. -/
def sl3IntGeneratedByOrderTwoAndThree : Prop :=
  ∃ a b : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ, orderOf a = 2 ∧ orderOf b = 3 ∧
    Subgroup.closure {a, b} = ⊤

/--
**$\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ is not $(2,3)$-generated.** There are no $a, b \in
\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ such that $a$ has order $2$, $b$ has order $3$, and $a$ and $b$ generate
$\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$. Equivalently, $\mathrm{SL}_3(\mathbb{Z})$ is not a quotient of the
modular group $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \cong C_2 \ast C_3$.

This is the negative answer to Kourovka Notebook Problem 14.49 (M. Conder), due to Tamburini and
Zucca, and Nuzhin.

Source: E.
I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 14.49 (M. Conder); resolution:
M. C. Tamburini and P. Zucca, Rend. Lincei Mat. Appl. (9) 11 (2000), no. 1, 5-7; Ya. N. Nuzhin,
Math. Notes 70 (2001), no. 1-2, 71-78, Kourovka Archive, Problem 14.49 (answer: No, it is not;
SL_d(ℤ) is such a quotient for d ≥ 28).
-/
public theorem_wanted sl3IntGeneratedByOrderTwoAndThree_refuted :
    ¬ sl3IntGeneratedByOrderTwoAndThree

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SL3IntTwoThreeGenerationKourovka14Problem49Wanted
